	"descriptionMarkdown": " Here is my Nauvis stationary space platform, steady 1,200spm.\n\nIt is based on \nMichael Hendriks' design (see https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cnm9fwJ_R5Q), but using endgame legendary modules, foundries, crushers, beacons, and assemblers, in order to save space.\n\nThere are two possible approaches for iron: you can convert ore into plates via foundries, or electric furnaces. I am not sure which design implies the smallest possible platform. With furnaces you can convert oxide asteroids into pure ice, which has a better yield, but with furnaces you use way less metallic asteroids, leaving more to be reprocessed into oxide asteroids (which are the ultimate bottleneck).\n\nThe final design is not as big as I thought it would end up being, and I am sure it is possible to be even smaller, as I am still throwing away some resources.",
